# SystemVerilog Operators – Complete Example

```systemverilog
module operators;

  int a = 10;
  int b = 3;

  logic [3:0] x = 4'b1010;
  logic [3:0] y = 4'b1100;

  logic p = 1'b1;
  logic q = 1'b0;

  initial begin

    // ============================================================
    // 1. ARITHMETIC OPERATORS
    // ============================================================

    $display("----- ARITHMETIC OPERATORS -----");

    $display("a + b = %0d", a + b);   // Addition
    $display("a - b = %0d", a - b);   // Subtraction
    $display("a * b = %0d", a * b);   // Multiplication
    $display("a / b = %0d", a / b);   // Division
    $display("a %% b = %0d", a % b);  // Modulus


    // ============================================================
    // 2. RELATIONAL OPERATORS
    // ============================================================

    $display("\n----- RELATIONAL OPERATORS -----");

    $display("a < b  = %0d", a < b);
    $display("a > b  = %0d", a > b);
    $display("a <= b = %0d", a <= b);
    $display("a >= b = %0d", a >= b);


    // ============================================================
    // 3. EQUALITY OPERATORS
    // ============================================================

    $display("\n----- EQUALITY OPERATORS -----");

    $display("a == b = %0d", a == b);
    $display("a != b = %0d", a != b);

    $display("x === y = %0d", x === y);
    $display("x !== y = %0d", x !== y);


    // ============================================================
    // 4. LOGICAL OPERATORS
    // ============================================================

    $display("\n----- LOGICAL OPERATORS -----");

    $display("p && q = %0d", p && q);   // Logical AND
    $display("p || q = %0d", p || q);   // Logical OR
    $display("!p     = %0d", !p);       // Logical NOT


    // ============================================================
    // 5. BITWISE OPERATORS
    // ============================================================

    $display("\n----- BITWISE OPERATORS -----");

    $display("x & y = %b", x & y);
    $display("x | y = %b", x | y);
    $display("x ^ y = %b", x ^ y);
    $display("x ~^ y = %b", x ~^ y);
    $display("x ^~ y = %b", x ^~ y);
    $display("~x = %b", ~x);


    // ============================================================
    // 6. SHIFT OPERATORS
    // ============================================================

    $display("\n----- SHIFT OPERATORS -----");

    $display("x << 1 = %b", x << 1);   // Logical left shift
    $display("x >> 1 = %b", x >> 1);   // Logical right shift
    $display("x <<< 1 = %b", x <<< 1); // Arithmetic left shift
    $display("x >>> 1 = %b", x >>> 1); // Arithmetic right shift


    // ============================================================
    // 7. INCREMENT / DECREMENT
    // ============================================================

    $display("\n----- INCREMENT / DECREMENT -----");

    $display("a = %0d", a);

    a++;
    $display("a++ = %0d", a);

    a--;
    $display("a-- = %0d", a);

    ++a;
    $display("++a = %0d", a);

    --a;
    $display("--a = %0d", a);


    // ============================================================
    // 8. ASSIGNMENT OPERATORS
    // ============================================================

    $display("\n----- ASSIGNMENT OPERATORS -----");

    a = 10;

    a += 5;
    $display("a += 5  -> %0d", a);

    a -= 5;
    $display("a -= 5  -> %0d", a);

    a *= 2;
    $display("a *= 2  -> %0d", a);

    a /= 2;
    $display("a /= 2  -> %0d", a);

    a %= 3;
    $display("a %%= 3 -> %0d", a);


    // ============================================================
    // 9. CONDITIONAL / TERNARY OPERATOR
    // ============================================================

    $display("\n----- CONDITIONAL OPERATOR -----");

    $display("Result = %0d", (a > b) ? a : b);


    // ============================================================
    // 10. CONCATENATION OPERATOR
    // ============================================================

    $display("\n----- CONCATENATION -----");

    $display("x = %b", x);
    $display("y = %b", y);
    $display("{x,y} = %b", {x,y});


    // ============================================================
    // 11. REPETITION OPERATOR
    // ============================================================

    $display("\n----- REPETITION -----");

    $display("{3{x}} = %b", {3{x}});


    // ============================================================
    // 12. INSIDE OPERATOR
    // ============================================================

    $display("\n----- INSIDE OPERATOR -----");

    if (a inside {[1:10]})
      $display("a is between 1 and 10");
    else
      $display("a is outside the range");


    // ============================================================
    // 13. SET MEMBERSHIP / ARRAY EXAMPLE
    // ============================================================

    int values[5] = '{10, 20, 30, 40, 50};

    $display("\n----- ARRAY -----");

    if (30 inside {values})
      $display("30 is present in array");


    // ============================================================
    // 14. EXPONENTIATION
    // ============================================================

    $display("\n----- EXPONENTIATION -----");

    $display("2 ** 3 = %0d", 2 ** 3);


    // ============================================================
    // 15. IMPLICATION OPERATORS
    // ============================================================
    // Mainly used in SystemVerilog Assertions (SVA)

    // |->  Overlapped implication
    // |=>  Non-overlapped implication

    // Example:
    //
    // property p;
    //   req |-> ack;
    // endproperty


    // ============================================================
    // 16. SVA SEQUENCE OPERATORS
    // ============================================================
    // These are used in assertions.

    // ##  -> Clock cycle delay
    // Example:
    //
    // req ##1 ack


    // ============================================================
    // 17. REDUCTION OPERATORS
    // ============================================================

    $display("\n----- REDUCTION OPERATORS -----");

    $display("&x  = %0d", &x);
    $display("|x  = %0d", |x);
    $display("^x  = %0d", ^x);
    $display("~&x = %0d", ~&x);
    $display("~|x = %0d", ~|x);
    $display("~^x = %0d", ~^x);
    $display("^~x = %0d", ^~x);


    // ============================================================
    // 18. LOGICAL REDUCTION / BOOLEAN EXAMPLE
    // ============================================================

    if (a && b)
      $display("Both a and b are non-zero");

    if (a || b)
      $display("At least one of a or b is non-zero");


    // ============================================================
    // 19. BIT SELECT
    // ============================================================

    $display("\n----- BIT SELECT -----");

    $display("x[0] = %b", x[0]);
    $display("x[3] = %b", x[3]);


    // ============================================================
    // 20. PART SELECT
    // ============================================================

    $display("\n----- PART SELECT -----");

    $display("x[3:2] = %b", x[3:2]);
    $display("x[1:0] = %b", x[1:0]);

  end

endmodule
/*
## Operator categories to remember

| Category            | Operators                             |   |    |
| ------------------- | ------------------------------------- | - | -- |
| Arithmetic          | `+ - * / % **`                        |   |    |
| Relational          | `< > <= >=`                           |   |    |
| Equality            | `== != === !==`                       |   |    |
| Logical             | `&&                                   |   | !` |
| Bitwise             | `& \| ^ ~ ^~ ~^`                      |   |    |
| Shift               | `<< >> <<< >>>`                       |   |    |
| Increment/Decrement | `++ --`                               |   |    |
| Assignment          | `= += -= *= /= %= <<= >>= &= \|= ^= ` |   |    |
| Conditional         | `?:`                                  |   |    |
| Concatenation       | `{}`                                  |   |    |
| Replication         | `{N{}}`                               |   |    |
| Reduction           | `& \| ^ ~& ~\| ~^ ^~`                 |   |    |
| Membership          | `inside`                              |   |    |
| Exponentiation      | `**`                                  |   |    |
| SVA implication     | `\|-> \|=>`                           |   |    |
| SVA delay           | `##`                                  |   |    |

### Most important distinction

For verification, pay special attention to these:

```text
==   → Logical equality
===  → Case equality (checks X/Z too)

&    → Bitwise AND
&&   → Logical AND

|    → Bitwise OR
||   → Logical OR

^    → Bitwise XOR / reduction XOR depending on operands
~^   → XNOR

<<   → Logical left shift
>>   → Logical right shift
<<<  → Arithmetic left shift
>>>  → Arithmetic right shift

=    → Blocking assignment
<=   → Non-blocking assignment
```

**Note:** `=` and `<=` are also assignment operators, but in RTL/verification code they have important procedural-assignment semantics beyond simply being arithmetic-style operators.

*/
